  "query_preview": "..\nThe outermost rainbands of Super Typhoon Champi (29W) brought sub-\nsevere thunderstorms across Guam and Rota as well as their adjacent \ncoastal waters, warranting Flood Advisories, various short-fuse\nWarnings, and Airport Weather Warnings throughout the day. Since \nthen, showers have stratified and cloud tops are no longer cooling, \nbut conditions remain unstable this evening. Therefore, numerous \nshowers with locally heavy showers possible and isolated \nthunderstorms are forecast tonight, becoming scattered near midnight.\nIsolated showers will then return for Guam and Rota Tuesday. As for \nthe CNMI, scattered showers and isolated thunderstorms will become \nisolated showers near midnight and continuing through midweek as a \nridge builds in following Champi's exit, with the exception of a \ntrade-wind trough briefly entering the region Tuesday night. Gentle \nto moderate trades will return to the entire region Tuesday and \ncontinue through the forecast period. The zones remain split to \naccount for the different headlines and shower coverage tonight, but \nmay be combined during the next forecast update. As for the long- \nterm, several broad troughs may travel across the region from the\neast, bringing periods of scattered showers and isolated \nthunderstorms later this week. A drier regime could return early \nnext week.",
